# Global form controls (Debt-Optimizer-Pro / aprly)

When building or restyling UI in `artifacts/aprly`, keep a **single visual language** for interactive controls. Prefer shared components over one-off inline styles.

## Use shared components first

| Control | Preferred location | Notes |
|---------|-------------------|--------|
| Text / email fields | `src/components/shared/auth-form/AuthTextInput` | Marketing/auth forms |
| Password fields | `src/components/shared/auth-form/AuthPasswordInput` | Includes show/hide toggle |
| Checkbox | `src/components/shared/auth-form/AuthCheckbox` | Figma green marketing style |
| Radio (when added) | `src/components/shared/auth-form/` or `shared/` | Add when a screen needs radios |
| Pill / primary CTA | `src/components/shared/PillButton` | Landing, auth modals |
| Step progress | `src/components/shared/StepProgressPills` | `variant="audit"` for Figma pills |

Before adding new field markup, search `src/components/shared/` for an existing wrapper.

## Do not change lightly

- **Do not** restyle global shadcn primitives (`src/components/ui/input.tsx`, `checkbox.tsx`, `button.tsx`) for one feature — that risks regressions on pages already aligned to Figma.
- **Do** extend or add wrappers under `shared/` with design tokens (`--input-*`, `--primary-theme-*`, `--design-input-min-height-x1`).

## Migration strategy

1. Introduce or extend shared component on the **current** screen (e.g. Sign Up).
2. Migrate other surfaces **incrementally** (login, forgot password, dashboard) in separate tasks — not bundled unless requested.
3. When migrating, preserve ids, `autoComplete`, validation, and event handlers — **UI only**.

## Styling conventions

- Input height: `h-[var(--design-input-min-height-x1,52px)]` where Figma specifies 52px.
- Borders/focus/error: `auth-field-styles` tokens, not ad-hoc colors.
- Buttons: `rounded-full`, `primary-theme-500` for marketing CTAs unless Figma specifies otherwise.

## Border radius (important)

`--design-button-corner-radius` (150px) and Tailwind `rounded-sm` / `rounded-lg` scale from `--radius` — both produce **pill/circle** shapes on small controls. Do **not** use them for auth inputs or checkboxes.

| Control | Radius |
|---------|--------|
| Auth text/password inputs | explicit `rounded-[12px]` via `auth-field-styles` |
| Auth checkbox | explicit `rounded-[2px]` via `AuthCheckbox` |
| Pill / marketing CTA | `rounded-full` (`PillButton`) |

## When inline styles are OK

- Truly unique one-off layout (not a reusable control).
- Prototype behind a flag — still plan extraction to `shared/` before merge when the pattern repeats.
